From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] riched20: TxDraw forgets a scroll position the text no longer needs (7001)

A windowless RichEdit whose text is set while its view has no width
scrolls the caret, at the end of the text, into view by the whole text.
Drawn with ITextServices::TxDraw into a wider view, the text was laid
out again but kept that scroll position, so nothing or only the last
letter showed (Zoom's Join dialog, "Your name"). TxDraw now updates the
scroll range after relayout, as a change of the host's client rectangle
already did; text that still does not fit keeps its position.
---
diff --git a/dlls/riched20/txtsrv.c b/dlls/riched20/txtsrv.c
index b4ca766..0f13a78 100644
--- a/dlls/riched20/txtsrv.c
+++ b/dlls/riched20/txtsrv.c
@@ -192,6 +192,14 @@ HRESULT __thiscall fnTextSrv_TxDraw( ITextServices *iface, DWORD aspect, LONG in
     {
         editor_mark_rewrap_all( services->editor );
         wrap_marked_paras_dc( services->editor, dc, FALSE );
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_TXDRAW_KEEPS_SCROLL
+        /* Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 7001): the view has a new size, so a scroll position the
+         * text no longer needs goes, as when the host's client rectangle changes
+         * (TXTBIT_CLIENTRECTCHANGE). Text set while the view had no width scrolled the caret
+         * into view by the whole text, and a wider view then showed nothing of it (Zoom's
+         * "Your name" box showed its last letter). */
+        ME_UpdateScrollBar( services->editor );
+#endif
     }
 
     if (!services->editor->bEmulateVersion10 || services->editor->nEventMask & ENM_UPDATE)
